  "why": "Mazur's all-degree proof answers the statement in full; Terence Tao, the author of the 2020/2022 Acta result on this problem, publicly reconstructed and simplified it, which is a named expert's digested rewrite (F9), so Mazur's event is whole/digested despite the 'proof candidate' label and the lack of a journal. The AI role is generated: the author's page credits GPT-5.6 Pro with 'proof development' under human orchestration and selection, and Tao calls it 'the AI-generated proof'. Tao's digest is also whole/digested, as a rewrite of the same mathematics; its only credited system, Claude Opus 5, wrote the Lean formalisation, so its role is none (F12). The Lean repository and Alexeev's unseen repository formalise known results, so they score none. An's paper re-proves part of the result conditionally on the Mazur–Tao reduction, so it adds no new coverage: none, and the architecture suggestions are too thin to count as AI mathematics. Zhang's quadratic inequality implies the statement and is scored whole/unreviewed; Codex only formalised it. The pre-2024 full-proof claims are set aside: Sofi and Drury–Lin are withdrawn or refuted, and Schmieder, Agama and Petrov are not credible (no uptake, the field still treated the problem as open). Classical partial results are cases.",
  "doubts": "Mazur's manuscript PDF was not read, and his own pages still call it a 'proof candidate' pending specialist certification. Digestion rests on Tao's blog reconstruction, which says the AI proof 'was not human-digested to be in the form of a publication-ready preprint'. That is a close call between digested and unreviewed; I chose digested because Tao worked through and rebuilt the argument in public. The mid-range degrees rely on computer certificates. Zhang 2609.19126 could arguably be a 'stronger form' (variant), but because it implies the statement I scored it whole. Its proof was not read in full. The Zhang large-degree date conflicts with its arXiv identifier, but both readings fall after the snapshot.",
